{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-gh:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-gh:3f69c5494341d7b9cc100f0ef19e070a7d162308db20656b92c21404c72a1c6c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:55:43Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.34.linker.w0","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-gh","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-gh","title":"Period notes that add up: a whole-ISO-week Week → Quarter → Year → All-time tree with stats strips, parts tables, and reviews Bryan closes","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:55:43Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.34.linker.w0","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:55:43Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Every daily note's parent is its ISO week note, and the tree climbs week → quarter → year → all_time → org with no dangling links. bob creates each period note ahead of time from a deterministic scaffold and never edits a note it did not just create. Every week, quarter, year, and all-time note opens with a live stats strip — the Day strip's family: the same five facts as period totals, a typical line, root and type lanes, and a parts row of its child periods — and a live parts table that summarizes each child automatically, with or without an agent. Each note carries complete, versioned agent instructions, so \"Update 2026/2026-W45.md\" is a whole prompt: agents take every number from `bob periods brief` and save only through `bob periods draft`, which never overwrites Bryan's edits. gtd_daily.md runs a Monday weekly review plus calendar-anchored quarterly and yearly reviews, and the glossary and decision records name the new pieces.","design":"plan:202611/period_notes_and_stats_strips.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/period_notes_and_stats_strips.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
